# SELECT50 example: UMA-S-1.1 relaxed coordinate scan.
#
# SETUP
# Install ORCA 6 and ORCA External Tools with UMA support as described at the
# top of job_orca.inp: https://github.com/faccts/orca-external-tools
# Replace ProgExt with the full installed oet_client path (.exe on Windows).
# Start the server in another terminal and leave it running:
#   oet_server uma -b 127.0.0.1:20001 -n 4
# Adjust the CPU allocation and cuda/cpu selection for your installation.
#
# RUN
# Use a fresh directory with this input and molecule.xyz (angstrom).
# Set the final line's charge/multiplicity and EDIT THE SCAN DEFINITION below.
# ORCA scan atom indices start at ZERO: index 0 is the first XYZ atom.
# SELECT50 bond-table indices start at ONE; subtract one when transferring them.
# The active example scans atoms 0 and 1 from 1.2 to 2.4 angstrom in 13 steps;
# these are illustrative values, not an assignment for your molecule.
# Choose a starting geometry close to the first requested scan coordinate.
#   /path/to/orca job_orca_scan.inp > job_orca_scan.out 2>&1
# Windows PowerShell:
#   & "C:/path/to/orca.exe" job_orca_scan.inp > job_orca_scan.out 2>&1
#
# Each point optimizes the other degrees of freedom. This input does not request
# frequencies at every point. Inspect convergence, energies and structures;
# a scan maximum can provide a TS guess but is not itself a verified TS.
# Replace the active B line with an A or D line for an angular scan (degrees),
# for example: A 0 1 2 = 100.0, 140.0, 21
#          or D 0 1 2 3 = -180.0, 180.0, 37
# Adding another active line creates a multidimensional scan by default.
# This is a derived template, not an original record of a deposited scan.
# Scan keywords: https://www.faccts.de/docs/orca/6.1/manual/contents/structurereactivity/optimizations_scans.html
#
! ExtOpt TightOpt

%method
  ProgExt "/path/to/oet_client"
  Ext_Params "-b 127.0.0.1:20001 --model uma-s-1p1 --task omol --device cuda"
end

%pal
  nprocs 4
end

%geom
  MaxStep 0.2
  MaxIter 1000
  Scan
    B 0 1 = 1.2, 2.4, 13
  end
end

* xyzfile 0 1 molecule.xyz
